      "better_line": "Decline to cast Alchemist's Gift and take 1 damage from Blisterpod. Save the combat trick for a situation where it can actually impact combat, such as giving deathtouch to a blocker against Thrashing Brontodon or enabling a profitable attack.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 113,
      "player": "Kimi25 Tactic",
      "decision_index": 105,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Stab Wound on Drowsing Tyrannodon is dealing 2 life per upkeep (already dropped from 19 to 13) and shrinking the Tyrannodon to 1/1. Thrashing Brontodon can destroy it right now for {1} + sacrifice, and the sick Forest can still tap for mana since mana abilities ignore summoning sickness. Brontodon wasn't enabling Tyrannodon to attack anyway (power 3, not 4+).",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Thrashing Brontodon's ability to destroy Stab Wound.",
      "better_line": "Activate Thrashing Brontodon ({1}, sacrifice) targeting Stab Wound to stop the 2 life per turn drain and restore Drowsing Tyrannodon to 3/3.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 114,
      "player": "Grk41F Timmy",
      "decision_index": 106,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Cast Alchemist's Gift during opponent's combat with no untapped creatures to block. The spell has no meaningful target here - there's no creature that can benefit from deathtouch or lifelink in this combat since Nightshade Stinger is tapped and can't block anyway. This wastes a card that could have been very valuable later (e.g., giving deathtouch to an attacker to force favorable trades, or lifelink in a race situation).",
      "action_taken": "Cast Alchemist's Gift during opponent's attack with Blisterpod, with no available blocker.",
      "better_line": "Decline to cast Alchemist's Gift (take the 1 damage from Blisterpod) and save it for a future combat where it could enable a favorable trade or provide meaningful lifelink.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 115,
      "player": "Kimi25 Tactic",
      "decision_index": 107,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Stab Wound is enchanting Drowsing Tyrannodon (reduced to 1/1 from 3/3), causing Grk41F Timmy to lose 2 life each upkeep. At 13 life, this recurring drain is very significant. Thrashing Brontodon can sacrifice for exactly {1} (paid by the untapped Forest) to destroy Stab Wound, stopping the life drain immediately. The Brontodon is summoning sick so it can't attack this turn anyway, and while losing it removes the power 4+ enabler for Tyrannodon, stopping 2 life per turn is far more important.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Thrashing Brontodon, leaving Stab Wound on Drowsing Tyrannodon.",
      "better_line": "Activate Thrashing Brontodon ({1}, sacrifice) targeting Stab Wound to stop the 2 life per upkeep drain and restore Drowsing Tyrannodon to 3/3.",
      "type": "blunder",
